[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3621814507","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113697#issuecomment-3621814507","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113697","id":3621814507,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7X4IDr","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-07T08:25:48Z","updated_at":"2025-12-07T08:27:23Z","body":"> However, this makes me wonder if this shouldn't be structured data instead?\r\n\r\n100% :slightly_smiling_face:\r\n\r\nRegex was _the way_ for `extension_interface.h`, but with the JSON, we should make use of structure as much as possible.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n\r\n> It could maybe be:\r\n> \r\n> ```jsonc\r\n> {\r\n>   // ...\r\n>   \"deprecated\": {\r\n>     \"since\": \"4.5\",\r\n>     \"message\": \"Use mem_alloc2 instead.\"\r\n>   }\r\n> }\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nThis looks like a great start.\r\n\r\nRegarding a potential `replace_with`, Kotlin has this in the form of [`@Deprecated` annotations](https://kotlinlang.org/api/core/kotlin-stdlib/kotlin/-deprecated/). This is tailored to automate IDE replacements, in cases where changing the expression is enough:\r\n```kotlin\r\n@Deprecated(\"Now obsolete\", ReplaceWith(\"better(i)\", \"org.acme.better\"), DeprecationLevel.WARNING)\r\nfun good(i: Int) { ... }\r\n```\r\n(There's also imports, and the level which can be increased to `ERROR`, e.g. in new major versions.)\r\n\r\nWe would not need that granularity, but one use case I see is automating links to docs.\r\nSo if we had:\r\n```jsonc\r\n{\r\n  // for function `mem_alloc`\r\n  \"deprecated\": {\r\n    \"since\": \"4.6\",\r\n    \"message\": \"Does not take into account padding.\",\r\n    \"replace_with\": \"mem_alloc2\" // <- optional field\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nWe could then generate links to the replacement in Doxygen/Sphinx/Rustdoc/... It's a small convenience, but if it's not too complicated to implement, might be nice :wink: ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3621814507/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3621953846","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113697#issuecomment-3621953846","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113697","id":3621953846,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7X4qE2","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-07T12:00:41Z","updated_at":"2025-12-07T12:00:41Z","body":"@Bromeon Thanks for the feedback!\r\n\r\nI've switched over to using structured data in my latest push :-)\r\n\r\nI ended up only making \"since\" required, because retroactively writing all the \"message\"s would be onerous. Later, if we want, we can fill them in and make it required.\r\n\r\nAlso, the Python code validates that the replacement actually exists and that it isn't deprecated too, which should help to prevent errors. It even found one error right away, which I think already justifies switching to structured data!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3621953846/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3632933291","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113697#issuecomment-3632933291","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113697","id":3632933291,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Yiimr","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-09T15:43:12Z","updated_at":"2025-12-09T15:43:28Z","body":"> to double-check, the current logic still adds the deprecation comment in all the possible places, right?\r\n\r\nYep! The messages just look a little bit different:\r\n\r\n```c++\r\ntypedef struct {\r\n\t...\r\n} GDExtensionClassCreationInfo; /* Deprecated in Godot 4.2. Use `GDExtensionClassCreationInfo4` instead. */\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * @name classdb_construct_object\r\n * @since 4.1\r\n * @deprecated Deprecated in Godot 4.4. Use `classdb_construct_object2` instead.\r\n *\r\n * ...\r\n */\r\ntypedef GDExtensionObjectPtr (*GDExtensionInterfaceClassdbConstructObject)(...);\r\n```\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3632933291/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3633259601","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113697#issuecomment-3633259601","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113697","id":3633259601,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YjyRR","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.co